SimplicialComplexes -- exploring abstract simplicial complexes within commutative algebra
*****************************************************************************************

Description
===========

An abstract simplicial complex (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_simplicial_complex ) is a family of
finite sets closed under the operation of taking subsets. In this package, the
finite set consists of variables in a *note polynomial ring:
(Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing, and each subset is represented as a product of
the corresponding variables.  In other words, we exploit the natural bijection
between abstract simplicial complexes and Stanley-Reisner ideals (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanley–Reisner_ring ).

This package is designed to explore applications of abstract simplicial
complexes within combinatorial commutative algebra. Introductions to this
theory can be found in the following textbooks:

  * Winfried Bruns (see https://www.home.uni-osnabrueck.de/wbruns/ ) and Jürgen
    Herzog (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jürgen_Herzog ), Cohen-Macaulay
    rings (see https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cohenmacaulay-rings/
    938BC2204D8A7C99E2CEBA1695A692A4 ), Cambridge Studies in Advanced
    Mathematics 39,Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, 1993. ISBN:
    0-521-41068-1
  * Ezra Miller (see https://services.math.duke.edu/~ezra/ ) and Bernd
    Sturmfels (see https://math.berkeley.edu/~bernd/ ), Combinatorial
    commutative algebra (see https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780387223568 ),
    Graduate Texts in Mathematics 227, Springer-Verlag, New York, 2005. ISBN:
    0-387-22356-8
  * Irena Peeva (see http://pi.math.cornell.edu/~irena/ ), Graded Syzygies (see
    https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-85729-177-6 ), Algebra and Applications 14,
    Springer-Verlag, London, 2011. ISBN: 978-0-85729-176-9
  * Richard Stanley (see http://www-math.mit.edu/~rstan/ ), Combinatorics and
    commutative algebra (see https://www.springer.com/gp/book/9780817643690 ),
    Progress in Mathematics 41, Birkhäuser Boston, Inc., Boston, MA, 1983.
    ISBN: 0-8176-3112-7

Contributors
============

The following people have generously contributed code, improved existing code,
or enhanced the documentation: Janko Böhm (see
https://www.mathematik.uni-kl.de/~boehm/ ), Sorin Popescu (see
https://www.math.stonybrook.edu/~sorin/ ), Mike Stillman (see
http://www.math.cornell.edu/~mike/ ), and Lorenzo Venturello (see
https://www.mis.mpg.de/nlalg/nlalg-people/lorenzo-venturello.html ).

Caveat
======

This package is not intended to handle abstract simplicial complexes with a
very large number of vertices, because computations in the corresponding
polynomial ring are typically prohibitive.

