barycentricSubdivision(SimplicialMap,Ring,Ring) -- create the map between barycentric subdivisions corresponding to a simplicial map
************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note barycentricSubdivision:
    barycentricSubdivision_lpSimplicialComplex_cmRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        barycentricSubdivision(f, R, S)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of abstract simplicial complexes: SimplicialMap,, from
        the simplicial complex $D$ to the simplicial complex $E$
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ambient ring for the
        barycentric subdivision of $E$
      * S, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ambient ring for the
        barycentric subdivision of $D$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of abstract simplicial complexes: SimplicialMap,, from the
        barycentric subdivision of $D$ to the barycentric subdivision of $E$.

Description
===========

The vertices of the barycentric subdivision of $D$ correspond to faces of $D$.
For every face $F$ in $D$, $\operatorname{barycentricSubdivision} (f,R,S)$ maps
the vertex corresponding to $F$ in the barycentric subdivision of $D$ to the
vertex corresponding to $f(F)$ in the barycentric subdivision of $E$. We work
out these correspondences, and the resulting simplicial map between barycentric
subdivisions in the example below.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = ZZ/2[x_0,x_1,x_2];                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplicialComplex{T_1*T_2}                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | x_1x_2 |                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Γ = simplicialComplex{T_0*T_1}                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = simplicialComplex | x_0x_1 |                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = map(Γ, Δ, reverse gens T)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | x_2 x_1 x_0 |                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | x_0x_1 | <--- simplicialComplex |     |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1x_2 |                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The barycentric subdivisions of $D$, $E$, and $f$ are:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = ZZ/2[y_0..y_2];                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : S = ZZ/2[z_0..z_2];                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : BΔ = barycentricSubdivision(Δ, R)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = simplicialComplex | y_1y_2 y_0y_2 |                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : BΓ = barycentricSubdivision(Γ, S)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = simplicialComplex | z_1z_2 z_0z_2 |                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o8 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : Bf = barycentricSubdivision(f, S, R)                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = | z_1 z_0 z_2 |                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | z_1z_2 z_0z_2 | <--- simplicialComplex|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|| y_1y_2 y_0y_2 |                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

In order to understand the data for $Bf$, we first look at the correspondence
between the faces of $\Delta$, $\Gamma$, and the vertices of $B\Delta$,
$B\Gamma$, respectively.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : ΔFaces = flatten for i to dim Δ + 1 list faces(i, Δ)               |
|                                                                         |
|o10 = {x , x , x x }                                                     |
|        1   2   1 2                                                      |
|                                                                         |
|o10 : List                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : ΓFaces = flatten for i to dim Γ + 1 list faces(i, Γ)               |
|                                                                         |
|o11 = {x , x , x x }                                                     |
|        0   1   0 1                                                      |
|                                                                         |
|o11 : List                                                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : netList transpose {for y in vertices BΔ list y => ΔFaces_(index y),|
|          for z in vertices BΓ list z => ΓFaces_(index z)}               |
|                                                                         |
|      +----------+----------+                                            |
|o12 = |y  => x   |z  => x   |                                            |
|      | 0     1  | 0     0  |                                            |
|      +----------+----------+                                            |
|      |y  => x   |z  => x   |                                            |
|      | 1     2  | 1     1  |                                            |
|      +----------+----------+                                            |
|      |y  => x x |z  => x x |                                            |
|      | 2     1 2| 2     0 1|                                            |
|      +----------+----------+                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+

These correspondences, together the images of each face of $D$ under $f$, will
completely determine the map $Bf$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : netList transpose {for F in ΔFaces list F => (map f)(F),               |
|          for v in vertices BΔ list v => (map Bf)(v) }                       |
|                                                                             |
|      +------------+--------+                                                |
|o13 = |x  => x     |y  => z |                                                |
|      | 1     1    | 0     1|                                                |
|      +------------+--------+                                                |
|      |x  => x     |y  => z |                                                |
|      | 2     0    | 1     0|                                                |
|      +------------+--------+                                                |
|      |x x  => x x |y  => z |                                                |
|      | 1 2     0 1| 2     2|                                                |
|      +------------+--------+                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : Bf                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o14 = | z_1 z_0 z_2 |                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o14 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | z_1z_2 z_0z_2 | <---                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|simplicialComplex | y_1y_2 y_0y_2 |                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note barycentricSubdivision(SimplicialComplex,Ring):
    barycentricSubdivision_lpSimplicialComplex_cmRing_rp, -- create the
    barycentric subdivision of a simplicial complex
  * *note SimplicialComplex: SimplicialComplex, -- the class of all abstract
    simplicial complexes

