complex(SimplicialComplex) -- create the chain complex associated to a simplicial complex.
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note complex: (Complexes)complex_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        complex Delta
        complex(Delta, Labels => L)
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Labels => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {}, L of
        monomials in a polynomial ring, one for each vertex of $\Delta$
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, of free modules

Description
===========

Each abstract simplicial complex $\Delta$ determines a chain complex of free
modules over its *note coefficient ring:
coefficientRing_lpSimplicialComplex_rp,.  For all integers $i$, the $i$-th
module in this chain complex has a basis corresponding to the $i$-dimensional
faces in the simplicial complex $\Delta$.

When the argument $\mathrm{Labels}$ has the default value, this method function
constructs $\widetilde C(D;k)$, where $k$ is the *note coefficient ring:
coefficientRing_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, of $\Delta$. The reduced homology of an
abstract simplicial complex $\Delta$ is, by definition, the homology of this
chain complex.  We illustrate this method with a triangulation of the torus and
Klein bottle.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[a..g];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : torus = smallManifold(2, 7, 6, S)                                       |
|                                                                             |
