dunceHatComplex(PolynomialRing) -- make a realization of the dunce hat with 8 vertices
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note dunceHatComplex: dunceHatComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        dunceHatComplex S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, that has at
        least 8 generators
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

The dunce hat (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dunce_hat_(topology) ) is a
compact topological space formed by taking a solid triangle and gluing all
three sides together, with the orientation of one side reversed. Simply gluing
two sides oriented in the same direction would yield a cone much like the dunce
cap, but the gluing of the third side results in identifying the base of the
cap with a line joining the base to the point.

Following Erik Christopher Zeeman's "On the dunce hat", Topology 2 (1964)
341–358, this method returns non-collapsible (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collapse_(topology) ) but contractible (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contractible_space ) example of an abstract
simplicial complex.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..h];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = dunceHatComplex S                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | fgh agh dfh cdh bch abh cfg bcg abg def aef acf bde |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|bce ace acd abd |                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : dim Δ                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = 2                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : fVector Δ                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {1, 8, 24, 17}                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(dim Δ === 2 and isPure Δ)                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(fVector Δ === {1,8,24,17})                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Our enumeration of the vertices follows the dunce hat (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/dunce_hat_eng.html )
example in Masahiro Hachimori's simplicial complex library (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/index_eng.html ).

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note rudinBallComplex: rudinBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a
    nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 41 facets
  * *note grunbaumBallComplex: grunbaumBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make
    a nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 29 facets
  * *note isPure(SimplicialComplex): isPure_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether
    the facets are equidimensional

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note dunceHatComplex(PolynomialRing): dunceHatComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
    -- make a realization of the dunce hat with 8 vertices
