Finding attributes and properties -- information about accessing features of an abstract simplicial complex
***********************************************************************************************************

Having made a *note SimplicialComplex: SimplicialComplex,, one can access its
basic invariants or test for some elementary properties by using the following
methods:

Determining attributes and properties of simplicial complexes
=============================================================

  * *note ideal(SimplicialComplex): ideal_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    Stanley–Reisner ideal
  * *note monomialIdeal(SimplicialComplex):
    monomialIdeal_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the Stanley–Reisner monomial
    ideal
  * *note ring(SimplicialComplex): ring_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    polynomial ring of its Stanley–Reisner ideal
  * *note coefficientRing(SimplicialComplex):
    coefficientRing_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the coefficient ring of the
    underlying polynomial ring
  * *note dim(SimplicialComplex): dim_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- find the
    dimension of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note facets(SimplicialComplex): facets_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    list of maximal faces
  * *note isPure(SimplicialComplex): isPure_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether
    the facets are equidimensional
  * *note vertices(SimplicialComplex): vertices_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get
    the list of the vertices for an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note faces(ZZ,SimplicialComplex): faces_lpZZ_cmSimplicialComplex_rp, --
    get the $i$-faces of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note connectedComponents(SimplicialComplex):
    connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- find the connected
    components of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note fVector(SimplicialComplex): fVector_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, --
    compute the f-vector of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note flagfVector(List,SimplicialComplex):
    flagfVector_lpList_cmSimplicialComplex_rp, -- compute a flag $f$-number of
    a colored simplicial complex
  * *note isProper(SimplicialComplex): isProper_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, --
    whether an abstract simplicial complex is properly colored

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note Working with associated chain complexes: Working with associated
    chain complexes, -- information about the chain complexes and their
    homogenizations
  * *note Working with simplicial maps: Working with simplicial maps, --
    information about simplicial maps and the induced operations
