grunbaumBallComplex(PolynomialRing) -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 29 facets
************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note grunbaumBallComplex:
    grunbaumBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        grunbaumBallComplex S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, that has at
        least 14 generators
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

Attributed to F. Alberto Grünbaum, this method returns a triangulation of a
3-ball with 14 vertices and 29 facets that is not shellable (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelling_(topology) ).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..s];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = grunbaumBallComplex S;                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : matrix {facets Δ}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | hlmn elmn gkmn fkmn ghmn efmn bhln beln ghjn fhjn bfhn befn agkm afkm |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     ghim egim aegm aefm aghj dfhj adhj bghi cegi bcgi abgh bdfh abdh aceg   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     abcg |                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|             1      29                                                       |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : dim Δ                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : fVector Δ                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {1, 14, 54, 70, 29}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(dim Δ === 3 and isPure Δ)                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(fVector Δ === {1,14,54,70,29})                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This abstract simplicial complex is Cohen-Macaulay but not shellable.

Our enumeration of the vertices follows the gruenbaum (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/gruenbaum_eng.html )
example in Masahiro Hachimori's simplicial complex library (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/index_eng.html ).

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note rudinBallComplex: rudinBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a
    nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 41 facets
  * *note zieglerBallComplex: zieglerBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a
    nonshellable 3-ball with 10 vertices and 21 facets
  * *note isPure(SimplicialComplex): isPure_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether
    the facets are equidimensional

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note grunbaumBallComplex(PolynomialRing):
    grunbaumBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with
    14 vertices and 29 facets
