ideal(SimplicialComplex) -- get the Stanley–Reisner ideal
*********************************************************

  * Function: *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)ideal,
  * Usage: 
        ideal Delta
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, that is generated by the
        monomials representing the minimal nonfaces in $\Delta$

Description
===========

In this package, an abstract simplicial complex is represented as squarefree
monomial ideal in a *note polynomial ring: ring_lpSimplicialComplex_rp,.  This
method function returns the defining ideal.

The boundary of the 4-simplex is a simplicial sphere with 5 vertices, 5
tetrahedral facets, and a minimal nonface that corresponds to the interior of
the sphere.

+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ[a..e];                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplicialComplex {b*c*d*e, a*c*d*e, a*b*d*e, a*b*c*e, a*b*c*d}|
|                                                                        |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | bcde acde abde abce abcd |                     |
|                                                                        |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal Δ                                                        |
|                                                                        |
|o3 = ideal(a*b*c*d*e)                                                   |
|                                                                        |
|o3 : Ideal of S                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : dim Δ                                                              |
|                                                                        |
|o4 = 3                                                                  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert (I == ideal a*b*c*d*e and instance(I, Ideal) and            |
|         numgens I === 1 and dim Δ === 3)                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The abstract simplicial complex from Example 1.8 of Miller-Sturmfels'
Combinatorial Commutative Algebra consists of a triangle (on vertices $a$, $b$,
$c$), two edges (connecting $c$ to $d$ and $b$ to $d$), and an isolated vertex
(namely $e$). It has six minimal nonfaces.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Γ = simplicialComplex {e, c*d, b*d, a*b*c}             |
|                                                            |
|o6 = simplicialComplex | e cd bd abc |                      |
|                                                            |
|o6 : SimplicialComplex                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : J = ideal Γ                                            |
|                                                            |
|o7 = ideal (a*d, b*c*d, a*e, b*e, c*e, d*e)                 |
|                                                            |
|o7 : Ideal of S                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert (J == ideal (a*d, b*c*d, a*e, b*e, c*e, d*e) and|
|         dim Γ === 2 and instance(J, Ideal))                |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

The irrelevant complex has the empty set as a facet whereas the void complex
has no facets.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : irrelevant = simplicialComplex {1_S};             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : M = ideal irrelevant                             |
|                                                       |
|o10 = ideal (a, b, c, d, e)                            |
|                                                       |
|o10 : Ideal of S                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert (M == ideal gens S and instance(M, Ideal))|
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : void = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal 1_S       |
|                                                       |
|o12 = simplicialComplex 0                              |
|                                                       |
|o12 : SimplicialComplex                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : U = ideal void                                   |
|                                                       |
|o13 = ideal 1                                          |
|                                                       |
|o13 : Ideal of S                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert (U == ideal 1_S and instance (U, Ideal))  |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

This routine is identical to *note monomialIdeal(SimplicialComplex):
monomialIdeal_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, except for the *note type:
(Macaulay2Doc)Type, of the output.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : printWidth = 250;                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : code (ideal, SimplicialComplex)                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o16 = -- code for method: ideal(SimplicialComplex)                           |
|      ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/SimplicialComplexes/Code.m2:19:36-19:|
|      ideal SimplicialComplex := Ideal => D -> ideal D.monomialIdeal         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|62: --source code:                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : code (monomialIdeal, SimplicialComplex)                                |
|                                                                             |
|o17 = -- code for method: monomialIdeal(SimplicialComplex)                   |
|      ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/SimplicialComplexes/Code.            |
|      monomialIdeal SimplicialComplex := MonomialIdeal => D -> D.            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|m2:20:52-20:72: --source code:                                               |
|monomialIdeal                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

As the Stanley–Reisner ideal is part the defining data of an abstract
simplicial complex, so this method does no computation.

See also
========

  * *note Finding attributes and properties: Finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note simplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal):
    simplicialComplex_lpMonomialIdeal_rp, -- make a simplicial complex from its
    Stanley–Reisner ideal
  * *note monomialIdeal(SimplicialComplex):
    monomialIdeal_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the Stanley–Reisner monomial
    ideal
  * *note facets(SimplicialComplex): facets_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    list of maximal faces
  * *note ring(SimplicialComplex): ring_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    polynomial ring of its Stanley–Reisner ideal

Ways to use this method:
========================

