isPure(SimplicialComplex) -- whether the facets are equidimensional
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note isPure: (Polyhedra)isPure,
  * Usage: 
        isPure Delta
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, which is true if the
        facets of $\Delta$ are of the same dimension, and false otherwise.

Description
===========

An abstract simplicial complex is pure of dimension $d$ if every facet has the
same dimension.

Many classic examples of abstract simplicial complexes are pure.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ[x_1..x_18];             |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : isPure simplexComplex(5, S)    |
|                                    |
|o2 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : isPure bartnetteSphereComplex S|
|                                    |
|o3 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : isPure bjornerComplex S        |
|                                    |
|o4 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : isPure dunceHatComplex S       |
|                                    |
|o5 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+
|i6 : isPure poincareSphereComplex S |
|                                    |
|o6 = true                           |
+------------------------------------+

The abstract simplicial complex from Example 1.8 of Miller-Sturmfels'
Combinatorial Commutative Algebra consists of a triangle (on vertices $a$, $b$,
$c$), two edges (connecting $c$ to $d$ and $b$ to $d$), and an isolated vertex
(namely $e$). It has six minimal nonfaces.  Moreover, its 1-skeleton and
2-skeleton are not pure.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R = ZZ/101[a..f];                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : Γ = simplicialComplex {e, c*d, b*d, a*b*c}|
|                                               |
|o8 = simplicialComplex | e cd bd abc |         |
|                                               |
|o8 : SimplicialComplex                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isPure Γ                                  |
|                                               |
|o9 = false                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i10 : isPure skeleton (1, Γ)                   |
|                                               |
|o10 = false                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i11 : isPure skeleton (2, Γ)                   |
|                                               |
|o11 = false                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------+

There are two "trivial" simplicial complexes: the irrelevant complex has the
empty set as a facet whereas the void complex has no faces.  Both are pure.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : irrelevant = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal gens S|
|                                                         |
|o12 = simplicialComplex | 1 |                            |
|                                                         |
|o12 : SimplicialComplex                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : isPure irrelevant                                  |
|                                                         |
|o13 = true                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : void = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal 1_S         |
|                                                         |
|o14 = simplicialComplex 0                                |
|                                                         |
|o14 : SimplicialComplex                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : isPure void                                        |
|                                                         |
|o15 = true                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Finding attributes and properties: Finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note dim(SimplicialComplex): dim_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- find the
    dimension of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note facets(SimplicialComplex): facets_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    list of maximal faces
  * *note skeleton(ZZ,SimplicialComplex): skeleton_lpZZ_cmSimplicialComplex_rp,
    -- make a new simplicial complex generated by all faces of a bounded
    dimension

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isPure(SimplicialComplex): isPure_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether
    the facets are equidimensional
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

