isWellDefined(SimplicialComplex) -- whether underlying data is uncontradictory
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined Delta
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if underlying data unambiguously defines an
        abstract simplicial complex

Description
===========

In this package, a simplicial complex is represented by its Stanley–Reisner
ideal (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanley–Reisner_ring ). The vertices
are identified with a subset of the variables in a polynomial ring and each
face is identified with the product of the corresponding variables. A nonface
is any subset of the variables that does not belong to the simplicial complex
and each nonface is again identified with a product of variables. The
Stanley-Reisner ideal of a simplicial complex is generated by monomials
corresponding to its nonfaces.

This method determines whether the underlying data correctly defines an
abstract simplicial complex.  In particular, it verifies that the monomial
ideal is *note squarefee: (Macaulay2Doc)isSquareFree, and that the matrix of
facets are the maximal faces in the abstract simplicial complex.

The boundary of the 4-simplex is a simplicial sphere with 5 vertices, 5 facets,
and a minimal nonface that corresponds to the interior of the sphere.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ[a..e];                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal (a*b*c*d*e)|
|                                                    |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | bcde acde abde abce abcd | |
|                                                    |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assert isWellDefined Δ                         |
+----------------------------------------------------+

This method also checks the following aspects of the data structure:

  * the underlying *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, has the expected
    keys, namely ring, monomialIdeal, facets, and cache,
  * the value of the ring key is a *note PolynomialRing:
    (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,,
  * the value of the monomialIdeal key is a *note MonomialIdeal:
    (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,,
  * the ring of the monomialIdeal value equals the value of the ring key,
  * the value of the facets key is a *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List,,
  * the ring of each entry in facets equals the value of the ring key,
  * the value of the cache key is a *note CacheTable:
    (Macaulay2Doc)CacheTable,.

Abstract simplicial complexes created using the constructors in this package
will automatically be well-defined.  The primary purpose of this method is to
document the underlying data structure for developers.

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note simplicialComplex(List): simplicialComplex_lpList_rp, -- make an
    abstract simplicial complex from a list of faces
  * *note simplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal):
    simplicialComplex_lpMonomialIdeal_rp, -- make a simplicial complex from its
    Stanley–Reisner ideal

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isWellDefined(SimplicialComplex):
    isWellDefined_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether underlying data is
    uncontradictory
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in SimplicialComplexes/Documentation.m2:925:0.

File: SimplicialComplexes.info, Node: isWellDefined_lpSimplicialMap_rp, Next: kleinBottleComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, Prev: isWellDefined_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, Up: Top

isWellDefined(SimplicialMap) -- whether underlying data is uncontradictory
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of abstract simplicial complexes: SimplicialMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is *note true:
        (Macaulay2Doc)true, if underlying data unambiguously defines a
        simplicial map

Description
===========

Maps between simplicial complexes are well-defined if the image of every face
is contained in a face. In this package, vertices of abstract simplicial
complexes are identified with a subset of the variables in a fixed polynomial
ring and each face is identified with monomials in those variables.
Consequently, a map between simplicial complexes is given by a map between the
respective polynomial rings.

This method determines whether the underlying ring map correctly defines a
simplicial map. In particular, it checks if variables are sent to variables,
and that the image of each monomial corresponding to a face in the source
divides some monomial corresponding to a face in the target (i.e. the image of
a face is contained in a face).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/229[a,b,c,d];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : D = simplicialComplex{a*b*c, b*c*d}                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | bcd abc |                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : E = simplicialComplex{a*b, b*c}                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = simplicialComplex | bc ab |                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = map(E,D,{a,b,b,c})                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | a b b c |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | bc ab | <--- simplicialComplex | bcd  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|abc |                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isWellDefined f                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The constructors in this package have no guarantee to be well defined; the data
defining a simplicial map is a ring map between the corresponding polynomial
rings, which could have no relation to the two complexes. By making the current
debugging level greater than one, one gets some additional information about
the nature of the failure.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g = map(E,D,{b*c,c,c+a,1})                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = | bc c a+c 1 |                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | bc ab | <--- simplicialComplex | bcd  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|abc |                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isWellDefined g                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : debugLevel = 1;                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isWellDefined g                                                         |
|-- expected image of a vertex to be a vertex                                 |
|o9 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : h = map(E,D,{a,b,c,c})                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = | a b c c |                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | bc ab | <--- simplicialComplex | bcd |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|abc |                                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : isWellDefined h                                                        |
|-- expected image of a face to be a face                                     |
|o11 = false                                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This method also checks the following aspects of the data structure:

  * the underlying *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable, has the expected
    keys, namely source, target, map, and cache,
  * the value of the source key is a *note SimplicialComplex:
    SimplicialComplex,,
  * the value of the target key is a *note SimplicialComplex:
    SimplicialComplex,,
  * the value of the RingMap key is a *note RingMap: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,.
  * the value of the cache key is a *note CacheTable:
    (Macaulay2Doc)CacheTable,.
  * the underlying ring map source value equals the ring of the source value,
  * the underlying ring map target value equals the ring of the target value,
  * the coefficient ring of the source value equals the coefficient ring of the
    target value,

See also
========

  * *note Working with simplicial maps: Working with simplicial maps, --
    information about simplicial maps and the induced operations
  * *note map(SimplicialComplex,SimplicialComplex,Matrix):
    map_lpSimplicialComplex_cmSimplicialComplex_cmMatrix_rp, -- create a
    simplicial map between simplicial complexes
  * *note map(SimplicialComplex,SimplicialComplex,List):
    map_lpSimplicialComplex_cmSimplicialComplex_cmMatrix_rp, -- create a
    simplicial map between simplicial complexes

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isWellDefined(SimplicialMap): isWellDefined_lpSimplicialMap_rp, --
    whether underlying data is uncontradictory
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

