kleinBottleComplex(PolynomialRing) -- make a minimal triangulation of the Klein bottle
**************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note kleinBottleComplex: kleinBottleComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        kleinBottleComplex S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, that
        specifies the polynomial ring containing the Stanley–Reisner ideal
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, corresponding
        to a minimal triangulation of the Klein bottle

Description
===========

This function accesses Frank Lutz's database of all small triangulated
2-manifolds via the method *note smallManifold:
smallManifold_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmZZ_cmPolynomialRing_rp, to obtain the minimal
triangulation of the Klein bottle.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ[x_0..x_7];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : KleinBottle = kleinBottleComplex S                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | x_2x_6x_7 x_0x_6x_7 x_2x_5x_7 x_0x_5x_7 x_4x_5x_6   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_3x_5x_6 x_0x_4x_6 x_2x_3x_6 x_1x_4x_5 x_0x_3x_5 x_1x_2x_5 x_2x_3x_4        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1x_3x_4 x_0x_2x_4 x_0x_1x_3 x_0x_1x_2 |                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

From Theorem 6.3 in Chapter one of Munkres' Algebraic Topology (see
https://www.pearson.com/us/higher-education/product/Munkres-Topology-2nd-
Edition/9780131816299.html ) states that the first homology of the Klein bottle
should have rank one free part, and $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ torsion. The
second homology should be zero.

+-------------------------+
|i3 : prune HH KleinBottle|
|                         |
|o3 = cokernel | 2 |      |
|              | 0 |      |
|                         |
|     1                   |
|                         |
|o3 : Complex             |
+-------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note smallManifold(ZZ,ZZ,ZZ,PolynomialRing):
    smallManifold_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmZZ_cmPolynomialRing_rp, -- get a small manifold
    from the Frank Lutz database

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note kleinBottleComplex(PolynomialRing):
    kleinBottleComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a minimal triangulation of
    the Klein bottle
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

