lyubeznikResolution -- create the Lyubeznik resolution of an ordered set of monomials.
**************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lyubeznikResolution L
        lyubeznikResolution M
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of monomials in a polynomial
        ring, that minimally generate a monomial ideal.
      * M, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * MonomialOrder => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {}
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, the Lyubeznik resolution of
        $S/M$.

Description
===========

For a monomial ideal $M$ in a polynomial ring $S$, minimally generated by $L$,
the Lyubeznik resolution is a resolution of $S/M$ determined by a total
ordering of the minimal generators of $M$. It is the subcomplex of the Taylor
resolution of $M$ induced on the rooted faces. If $L$ is used as input, the
ordering is the order in which the monomials appear in $L$. If $M$ is used as
the input, the ordering is obtained from $\operatorname{first}
\operatorname{mingens} \operatorname{entries} M$. For more details on Lyubeznik
resolutions and their construction, see Jeff Mermin Three Simplicial
Resolutions (see https://www.degruyter.com/view/book/9783110250404/10.1515/
9783110250404.127.xml ), (English summary) Progress in commutative algebra 1,
127–141, de Gruyter, Berlin, 2012.

+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[x,y];                     |
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = monomialIdeal{x*y,x^2,y^3};  |
|                                      |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of S               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : F = lyubeznikResolution M;       |
+--------------------------------------+
|i4 : F.dd                             |
|                                      |
|          1                    3      |
|o4 = 0 : S  <---------------- S  : 1  |
|               | xy x2 y3 |           |
|                                      |
|          3                      2    |
|     1 : S  <------------------ S  : 2|
|               {2} | -x -y2 |         |
|               {2} | y  0   |         |
|               {3} | 0  x   |         |
|                                      |
|o4 : ComplexMap                       |
+--------------------------------------+

Changing the order of the generators may change the output. We can do this by
manually entering the permuted list of generators, or by using the optional
$\mathrm{MonomialOrder}$ argument.

+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : first entries mingens M                            |
|                                                        |
|            2   3                                       |
|o5 = {x*y, x , y }                                      |
|                                                        |
|o5 : List                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : F' = lyubeznikResolution({x^2,y^3,x*y});           |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : F'.dd                                              |
|                                                        |
|          1                    3                        |
|o7 = 0 : S  <---------------- S  : 1                    |
|               | x2 y3 xy |                             |
|                                                        |
|          3                         3                   |
|     1 : S  <--------------------- S  : 2               |
|               {2} | -y3 -y 0  |                        |
|               {3} | x2  0  -x |                        |
|               {2} | 0   x  y2 |                        |
|                                                        |
|          3                   1                         |
|     2 : S  <--------------- S  : 3                     |
|               {5} | 1   |                              |
|               {3} | -y2 |                              |
|               {4} | x   |                              |
|                                                        |
|o7 : ComplexMap                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : F' = lyubeznikResolution(M,MonomialOrder=>{1,2,0});|
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : F'.dd                                              |
|                                                        |
|          1                    3                        |
|o9 = 0 : S  <---------------- S  : 1                    |
|               | x2 y3 xy |                             |
|                                                        |
|          3                         3                   |
|     1 : S  <--------------------- S  : 2               |
|               {2} | -y3 -y 0  |                        |
|               {3} | x2  0  -x |                        |
|               {2} | 0   x  y2 |                        |
|                                                        |
|          3                   1                         |
|     2 : S  <--------------- S  : 3                     |
|               {5} | 1   |                              |
|               {3} | -y2 |                              |
|               {4} | x   |                              |
|                                                        |
|o9 : ComplexMap                                         |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note SimplicialComplexes: Top, -- exploring abstract simplicial complexes
    within commutative algebra
  * *note lyubeznikSimplicialComplex: lyubeznikSimplicialComplex, -- create a
    simplicial complex supporting a Lyubeznik resolution of a monomial ideal
  * *note taylorResolution: taylorResolution, -- create the Taylor resolution
    of a monomial ideal

Ways to use lyubeznikResolution:
================================

  * "lyubeznikResolution(List)"
  * "lyubeznikResolution(MonomialIdeal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note lyubeznikResolution: lyubeznikResolution, is a *note method
function with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

