Making an abstract simplicial complex -- information about the basic constructors
*********************************************************************************

An abstract simplicial complex on a finite set is a family of subsets that is
closed under taking subsets.  The elements in the abstract simplicial complex
are called its faces.  The faces having cardinality 1 are its vertices and the
maximal faces (order by inclusion) are its facets.  Following the combinatorial
conventions, every nonempty abstract simplicial complex has the empty set as a
face.

In this package, a simplicial complex is represented by its Stanley–Reisner
ideal (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanley–Reisner_ring ). The vertices
are identified with a subset of the variables in a polynomial ring and each
face is identified with the product of the corresponding variables. A nonface
is any subset of the variables that does not belong to the simplicial complex
and each nonface is again identified with product of variables. The
Stanley-Reisner ideal of a simplicial complex is generated by monomials
corresponding to its nonfaces.

Basic constructors for abstract simplicial complexes
====================================================

  * *note simplicialComplex(List): simplicialComplex_lpList_rp, -- make an
    abstract simplicial complex from a list of faces
  * *note simplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal):
    simplicialComplex_lpMonomialIdeal_rp, -- make a simplicial complex from its
    Stanley–Reisner ideal
  * *note SimplicialComplex: SimplicialComplex, -- the class of all abstract
    simplicial complexes
  * *note isWellDefined(SimplicialComplex):
    isWellDefined_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether underlying data is
    uncontradictory

Classic examples of abstract simplicial complexes
=================================================

  * *note simplexComplex(ZZ,PolynomialRing):
    simplexComplex_lpZZ_cmPolynomialRing_rp, -- make the simplex as an abstract
    simplicial complex
  * *note bartnetteSphereComplex(PolynomialRing):
    bartnetteSphereComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a non-polytopal
    3-sphere with 8 vertices
  * *note bjornerComplex(PolynomialRing): bjornerComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
    -- make a shellable 2-polyhedron with 6 vertices
  * *note dunceHatComplex(PolynomialRing): dunceHatComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
    -- make a realization of the dunce hat with 8 vertices
  * *note poincareSphereComplex(PolynomialRing):
    poincareSphereComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a homology 3-sphere with
    16 vertices
  * *note nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex(PolynomialRing):
    nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a
    non-piecewise-linear 5-sphere with 18 vertices
  * *note rudinBallComplex(PolynomialRing):
    rudinBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with 14
    vertices and 41 facets
  * *note grunbaumBallComplex(PolynomialRing):
    grunbaumBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with
    14 vertices and 29 facets
  * *note zieglerBallComplex(PolynomialRing):
    zieglerBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with
    10 vertices and 21 facets
  * *note smallManifold: smallManifold_lpZZ_cmZZ_cmZZ_cmPolynomialRing_rp, --
    get a small manifold from the Frank Lutz database

Other operations producing abstract simplicial complexes
========================================================

  * *note prune(SimplicialComplex): prune_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- make a
    minimal presentation of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note inducedSubcomplex(SimplicialComplex,List):
