map(SimplicialMap) -- the underlying ring map associated to a simplicial map
****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        phi = map f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of abstract simplicial complexes: SimplicialMap,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, =>
        ..., default value null, ignored
      * *note DegreeLift: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, ignored
      * *note DegreeMap: (Macaulay2Doc)map_lpRing_cmRing_cmMatrix_rp, => ...,
        default value null, ignored
  * Outputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, a map from the ring of
        the source of $f$ to the ring of the target of $f$.

Description
===========

Every simplicial map sends the vertices of the source of $f$ to the vertices of
the target of $f$. Consequently, this determines a ring map between the ring of
the source of $f$ and the ring of the target of $f$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d];                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplexComplex(3,S)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | abcd |                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = map(Δ,Δ,matrix{{a,b,c,d}})                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | a b c d |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : SimplicialMap simplicialComplex | abcd | <--- simplicialComplex | abcd ||
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : map f                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = map (S, S, {a, b, c, d})                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : RingMap S <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Working with simplicial maps: Working with simplicial maps, --
    information about simplicial maps and the induced operations
  * *note map(SimplicialComplex,SimplicialComplex,RingMap):
    map_lpSimplicialComplex_cmSimplicialComplex_cmMatrix_rp, -- create a
    simplicial map between simplicial complexes
  * *note source(SimplicialMap): source_lpSimplicialMap_rp, -- get the source
    of the map
  * *note target(SimplicialMap): target_lpSimplicialMap_rp, -- get the target
    of the map
  * *note matrix(SimplicialMap): matrix_lpSimplicialMap_rp, -- get the
    underlying map of rings
  * *note isWellDefined(SimplicialMap): isWellDefined_lpSimplicialMap_rp, --
    whether underlying data is uncontradictory

