net(SimplicialComplex) -- make a symbolic representation of an abstract simplicial complex
******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)net,
  * Usage: 
        net Delta
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)Net,, a symbolic representation used for
        printing

Description
===========

The net of an abstract simplicial complex is an expression that lists the
monomials representing the facets (also known as the maximal faces).  This
function is the primary function called upon by *note << Thing:
(Macaulay2Doc)printing to a file, to format for printing.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ[a..f];                                        |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal(a*f, b*d, c*e)   |
|                                                          |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | def bef cdf bcf ade abe acd abc ||
|                                                          |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : net Δ                                                |
|                                                          |
|o3 = simplicialComplex | def bef cdf bcf ade abe acd abc ||
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert instance(net Δ, Net)                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

The void complex has no facets whereas the irrelevant complex has the empty set
as a facet.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : void = simplicialComplex monomialIdeal 1_S|
|                                               |
|o5 = simplicialComplex 0                       |
|                                               |
|o5 : SimplicialComplex                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : net void                                  |
|                                               |
|o6 = simplicialComplex 0                       |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : irrelevant = simplicialComplex {1_S};     |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : net irrelevant                            |
|                                               |
|o8 = simplicialComplex | 1 |                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Finding attributes and properties: Finding attributes and properties,
    -- information about accessing features of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note facets(SimplicialComplex): facets_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- get the
    list of maximal faces

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note net(SimplicialComplex): net_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- make a
    symbolic representation of an abstract simplicial complex
