nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex(PolynomialRing) -- make a non-piecewise-linear 5-sphere with 18 vertices
********************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex:
    nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        nonPiecewiseLinearSphereComplex S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, that has at
        least 18 generators
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

A piecewise linear (PL) (see
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Piecewise_linear_manifold ) sphere is a manifold
which is PL homeomorphic to the boundary of a simplex. All the spheres in
dimensions less than or equal to 3 are PL, but there are non-PL spheres in
dimensions larger than or equal to 5.

As described in Theorem 7 in Anders Björner and Frank H. Lutz's "Simplicial
manifolds, bistellar flips and a 16-vertex triangulation of the Poincaré
homology 3-sphere", Experimental Mathematics 9 (2000) 275–289, this method
returns a non-PL 5-sphere constructed from the *note Björner–Lutz homology
sphere: poincareSphereComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, by taking a double
suspension.

