substitute(SimplicialComplex,PolynomialRing) -- change the ring of a simplicial complex
***************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note substitute: (Macaulay2Doc)substitute,
  * Usage: 
        substitute(Delta, R)
  * Inputs:
      * Delta, an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

Given a polynomial ring $R$, with enough variables, we can create a simplicial
complex identical to $\Delta$, defined over the ring $R$.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/23[x,y,z,w];       |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = simplexComplex(3,S)   |
|                               |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | xyzw ||
|                               |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex         |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d,e];    |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : Γ = substitute(Δ, R)      |
|                               |
|o4 = simplicialComplex | abcd ||
|                               |
|o4 : SimplicialComplex         |
+-------------------------------+

This method is a works by applying *note substitute(RingElement,Ring):
(Macaulay2Doc)substitute, to the facets of $\Delta$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : code(substitute, SimplicialComplex, PolynomialRing)                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = -- code for method: substitute(SimplicialComplex,PolynomialRing)        |
|     ../../../../../Macaulay2/packages/SimplicialComplexes/Code.m2:668:70-678|
|     :5: --source code:                                                      |
|     substitute(SimplicialComplex, PolynomialRing) := SimplicialComplex => (D|
|         if ideal D === ideal(1_(ring D))                                    |
|         then (                                                              |
|             I := sub(ideal D, R);                                           |
|             simplicialComplex monomialIdeal I                               |
|             )                                                               |
|         else (                                                              |
|             n := numgens ring D;                                            |
|             simplicialComplex for F in facets D list sub(F, (vars R)_{0..n-1|
|             )                                                               |
|         )                                                                   |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|, R) -> (                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|})                                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note substitute(SimplicialComplex,PolynomialRing):
    substitute_lpSimplicialComplex_cmPolynomialRing_rp, -- change the ring of a
    simplicial complex
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

