taylorResolution -- create the Taylor resolution of a monomial ideal
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        taylorResolution L
        taylorResolution M
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of monomials in a polynomial
        ring, that minimally generate a monomial ideal.
      * M, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

If $M$ is a monomial ideal, minimally generated by $L$, then the Taylor
resolution of $M$ is the resolution of $M$ obtained by homogenizing the $(\#L -
1)$-simplex.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = QQ[vars(0..3)]                                |
|                                                       |
|o1 = S                                                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = monomialIdeal(a*b,c^3,c*d,b^2*c)              |
|                                                       |
|                          2    3                       |
|o2 = monomialIdeal (a*b, b c, c , c*d)                 |
|                                                       |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of S                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T = taylorResolution M                            |
|                                                       |
|      1      4      6      4      1                    |
|o3 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S                     |
|                                                       |
|     0      1      2      3      4                     |
|                                                       |
|o3 : Complex                                           |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : T.dd                                              |
|                                                       |
|          1                        4                   |
|o4 = 0 : S  <-------------------- S  : 1               |
|               | cd ab c3 b2c |                        |
|                                                       |
|          4                                       6    |
|     1 : S  <----------------------------------- S  : 2|
|               {2} | -ab -c2 -b2 0   0   0   |         |
|               {2} | cd  0   0   -c3 -bc 0   |         |
|               {3} | 0   d   0   ab  0   -b2 |         |
|               {3} | 0   0   d   0   a   c2  |         |
|                                                       |
|          6                              4             |
|     2 : S  <-------------------------- S  : 3         |
|               {4} | c2  b  0   0   |                  |
|               {4} | -ab 0  b2  0   |                  |
|               {4} | 0   -a -c2 0   |                  |
|               {5} | d   0  0   b   |                  |
