Working with associated chain complexes -- information about the chain complexes and their homogenizations
**********************************************************************************************************

Each abstract simplicial complex $\Delta$ determines a chain complex of free
modules over its *note coefficient ring:
coefficientRing_lpSimplicialComplex_rp,. For all integers $i$, the $i$-th term
in this chain complex has a basis corresponding to the $i$-dimensional faces in
the simplicial complex $\Delta$.  The reduced homology of $\Delta$ is, by
definition, the homology of this chain complex.  Similarly, the reduced
cohomology of $\Delta$ is obtained by first using the $\operatorname{Hom}$
functor and then taking homology.

Basic operations arising of 
============================

  * *note complex(SimplicialComplex): complex_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- create
    the chain complex associated to a simplicial complex.
  * *note boundaryMap(ZZ,SimplicialComplex):
    boundaryMap_lpZZ_cmSimplicialComplex_rp, -- make a boundary map between the
    oriented faces of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note HH_ZZ SimplicialComplex: HH_usZZ_lpSimplicialComplex_cmRing_rp, --
    compute the reduced homology of an abstract simplicial complex
  * *note HH^ZZ SimplicialComplex: HH^ZZ_lpSimplicialComplex_cmRing_rp, --
    compute the reduced cohomology of an abstract simplicial complex

Constructing abstract simplicial complexes from monomial ideals
===============================================================

Monomial ideals produce a few different abstract simplicial complexes, where
the vertices are in bijection with the unique minimal set of monomial
generators.

  * *note buchbergerSimplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal,Ring):
    buchbergerSimplicialComplex, -- make the Buchberger complex of a monomial
    ideal
  * *note lyubeznikSimplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal,Ring):
    lyubeznikSimplicialComplex, -- create a simplicial complex supporting a
    Lyubeznik resolution of a monomial ideal
  * *note scarfSimplicialComplex(MonomialIdeal,Ring): scarfSimplicialComplex,
    -- create the Scarf simplicial complex for a list of monomials

Free chain complexes arising from abstract simplicial complexes
===============================================================

By labelling or identifying the vertices in an abstract simplicial complex with
distinct monomials (and each face with the least common multiple of its
vertices), one transforms a chain complex of vector spaces into chain complex
of free modules over a polynomial ring.  This approach allows one to understand
the minimal resolutions of some monomial ideals.

  * *note complex(SimplicialComplex,Labels=>...):
    complex_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- create the chain complex associated to a
    simplicial complex.
  * *note buchbergerResolution(MonomialIdeal): buchbergerResolution, -- make a
    Buchberger resolution of a monomial ideal
  * *note lyubeznikResolution(MonomialIdeal): lyubeznikResolution, -- create
    the Lyubeznik resolution of an ordered set of monomials.
  * *note scarfChainComplex(MonomialIdeal): scarfChainComplex, -- create the
    Scarf chain complex for a list of monomials.
  * *note taylorResolution(MonomialIdeal): taylorResolution, -- create the
    Taylor resolution of a monomial ideal

See also
========

