zieglerBallComplex(PolynomialRing) -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with 10 vertices and 21 facets
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note zieglerBallComplex: zieglerBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp,
  * Usage: 
        zieglerBallComplex S
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, that has at
        least 10 generators
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: SimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

As appears on page 167 of Günter M. Ziegler's "Shelling polyhedral 3-balls and
4-polytopes", Discrete & Computational Geometry 19 (1998) 159–174, this method
returns a non-shellable  (see https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shelling_(topology)
) 3-ball with 10 vertices and 21 facets.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..n];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Δ = zieglerBallComplex S;                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : matrix {facets Δ}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | bfgj bcgj befj abej abcj aehi adhi aefi abfi abdi cfgh degh cdgh bcfh |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     adeh bcdh bcfg adeg acdg abef abcd |                                    |
|                                                                             |
|             1      21                                                       |
|o3 : Matrix S  <-- S                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : dim Δ                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : fVector Δ                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {1, 10, 38, 50, 21}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(dim Δ === 3 and isPure Δ)                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(fVector Δ === {1,10,38,50,21})                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This abstract simplicial complex is Cohen-Macaulay but not shellable.

Our enumeration of the vertices follows the ziegler (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/ziegler_eng.html )
example in Masahiro Hachimori's simplicial complex library (see
http://infoshako.sk.tsukuba.ac.jp/~hachi/math/library/index_eng.html ).

See also
========

  * *note Making an abstract simplicial complex: Making an abstract simplicial
    complex, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note rudinBallComplex: rudinBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a
    nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 41 facets
  * *note grunbaumBallComplex: grunbaumBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make
    a nonshellable 3-ball with 14 vertices and 29 facets
  * *note isPure(SimplicialComplex): isPure_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, -- whether
    the facets are equidimensional

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note zieglerBallComplex(PolynomialRing):
    zieglerBallComplex_lpPolynomialRing_rp, -- make a nonshellable 3-ball with
    10 vertices and 21 facets
